flowchart TB
  accTitle: Organize current-branch history in Lazygit
  accDescr: Press i in Commits to start a current-branch interactive rebase. Use s or f on TODO commits, then continue through m. Use e to start editing from a selected commit. Coordinate changes to shared history.
  before["Before cleanup<br/>A feature commit plus WIP and fix commits"]
  select["Open Commits (4)<br/>Confirm the branch and history scope"]
  rebase["i · Rebase the current branch<br/>e · Edit from selected commit"]
  subgraph actions["Choose actions for TODO commits"]
    direction LR
    squash["s · squash<br/>Combine changes<br/>Keep commit messages"]
    fixup["f · fixup<br/>Combine changes<br/>Discard that commit's message"]
    squash ~~~ fixup
  end
  confirm["m · Open rebase options<br/>Select continue"]
  after["After cleanup<br/>Related changes form clear commits"]
  published["Inspect final history and tests<br/>Coordinate before updating shared history"]
  before --> select --> rebase
  rebase --> actions
  actions --> confirm
  confirm --> after --> published
